        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>Bug Description:
Orc cannot perform a melee attack when the Player is positioned
below the Orc, even though the Player is within the specified
35px attack range.

Precondition:
- Combat Room is active.
- Orc is alive and able to attack.
- Player is within 35px of the Orc.

Steps to Reproduce:
1. Enter a Combat Room containing an Orc.
2. Move the Player to a position below the Orc.
3. Keep the distance between Player and Orc &lt;= 35px.
4. Wait for the Orc to attack.

Expected Result:
Orc performs a melee attack against the Player when the Player
is within 35px, regardless of whether the Player is positioned
above or below the Orc.

Actual Result:
Orc does not perform the melee attack when the Player is below
the Orc.

Test Case:
TC-EN-XX</pre>
</div></div>
            <br/>
